, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the rotation $R$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\text{ }[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are \n\n$$\n(0,\\sqrt{2}),\\,(\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}},-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}),\\,(-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{2}},\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}).\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072578/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ea118cc3116902a9570a5568096ce1c598dcda978c888c4c69da173fca05ca3"} {"question" "q-11967" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072578/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bea49cac97e9ba0eeacea89fec567b1759c075ac7b74ca8370ffbb975e7f5996"} {"question" "q-11967" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072578/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ea118cc3116902a9570a5568096ce1c598dcda978c888c4c69da173fca05ca3"} {"question" "q-11967" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072578/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ea118cc3116902a9570a5568096ce1c598dcda978c888c4c69da173fca05ca3"} {"question" "q-11967" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072578/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ea118cc3116902a9570a5568096ce1c598dcda978c888c4c69da173fca05ca3"} {"question" "q-82050" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the geometrical interpretation of the transformation represented by the matrix $A$ given below? \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072578/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ea118cc3116902a9570a5568096ce1c598dcda978c888c4c69da173fca05ca3"} {"question" "q-82050" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The rotation matrix ${R}_{\\theta }$ represents a rotation of angle $\\theta $ counterclockwise about the origin and is given by\n\n$$\n{R}_{\\theta }=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nComparing $A$ with the rotation matrix, we have \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince both $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ are positive, we must have $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ \n\nDividing the first equation by the second gives\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =1.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A$ represents a rotation of $\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ radians anticlockwise about the origin." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072578/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ea118cc3116902a9570a5568096ce1c598dcda978c888c4c69da173fca05ca3"} {"question" "q-82050" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072578/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bea49cac97e9ba0eeacea89fec567b1759c075ac7b74ca8370ffbb975e7f5996"} {"question" "q-82050" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072578/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ea118cc3116902a9570a5568096ce1c598dcda978c888c4c69da173fca05ca3"} {"question" "q-82050" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A rotation of $\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ radians counterclockwise about the origin."] ["text" "A rotation of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians clockwise about the origin."] ["text" "A rotation of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians counterclockwise about the origin."] ["text" "A rotation of $\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ radians clockwise about the origin."] ["text" "A rotation of $\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ radians counterclockwise about the origin."]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072578/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ea118cc3116902a9570a5568096ce1c598dcda978c888c4c69da173fca05ca3"} {"question" "q-82050" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "A rotation of $\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ radians counterclockwise about the origin."] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072578/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ea118cc3116902a9570a5568096ce1c598dcda978c888c4c69da173fca05ca3"} {"question" "q-275762" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The vector $v=⟨-2,-2⟩$ is rotated ${45}^{∘}$ **clockwise** about the origin. Find the image of $v$ under this rotation.\n\n${v}^{′}=⟨$\n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}}\n$⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072578/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ea118cc3116902a9570a5568096ce1c598dcda978c888c4c69da173fca05ca3"} {"question" "q-275762" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A rotation of ${45}^{∘}$ *clockwise* about the origin is represented by the matrix \n\n$$\n{R}_{(-{45}^{∘})}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-{45}^{∘}) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-{45}^{∘}) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(-{45}^{∘}) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(-{45}^{∘})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image ${v}^{′}$ under the action of the matrix ${R}_{(-{45}^{∘})}$, we compute the matrix product, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}^{′} & ={R}_{(-{45}^{∘})}\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image is ${v}^{′}=⟨-2\\sqrt{2},0⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072578/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ea118cc3116902a9570a5568096ce1c598dcda978c888c4c69da173fca05ca3"} {"question" "q-275762" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072578/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bea49cac97e9ba0eeacea89fec567b1759c075ac7b74ca8370ffbb975e7f5996"} {"question" "q-275762" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072578/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ea118cc3116902a9570a5568096ce1c598dcda978c888c4c69da173fca05ca3"} {"question" "q-275762" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072578/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ea118cc3116902a9570a5568096ce1c598dcda978c888c4c69da173fca05ca3"} {"question" "q-275762" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072578/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ea118cc3116902a9570a5568096ce1c598dcda978c888c4c69da173fca05ca3"} {"question" "q-275762" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072578/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ea118cc3116902a9570a5568096ce1c598dcda978c888c4c69da173fca05ca3"} {"question" "q-279364" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The vector $v=⟨-4,-2⟩$ is rotated ${225}^{∘}$ **clockwise** about the origin. Find the image of $v$ under this rotation.\n\n${v}^{′}=⟨$\n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}}\n$⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072578/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ea118cc3116902a9570a5568096ce1c598dcda978c888c4c69da173fca05ca3"} {"question" "q-279364" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A rotation of ${225}^{∘}$ *clockwise* about the origin is represented by the matrix \n\n$$\n{R}_{(-{225}^{∘})}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-{225}^{∘}) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-{225}^{∘}) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(-{225}^{∘}) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(-{225}^{∘})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image ${v}^{′}$ under the action of the matrix ${R}_{(-{225}^{∘})}$, we compute the matrix product, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}^{′} & ={R}_{(-{225}^{∘})}\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{2} \\\\ -\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image is ${v}^{′}=⟨3\\sqrt{2},-\\sqrt{2}⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072578/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ea118cc3116902a9570a5568096ce1c598dcda978c888c4c69da173fca05ca3"} {"question" "q-279364" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072578/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bea49cac97e9ba0eeacea89fec567b1759c075ac7b74ca8370ffbb975e7f5996"} {"question" "q-279364" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072578/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ea118cc3116902a9570a5568096ce1c598dcda978c888c4c69da173fca05ca3"} {